<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $27.29 bln on May 9.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $27.29 bln on May 9.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $27.29 billion on May 9 from $26.65 billon a week ago, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  May 9	 May 2	  May 10</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     23,321	22,656	 17,271</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,966	 3,966	  4,520</p>
<p>    SDRs				    --	    26	     70</p>
<p>    Total			     27,287	26,648	 21,861</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
